        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects: Applications Technology Satellites (ATS)\n- Organizations: NASA\n- People: Wernher von Braun\n- Roles: aerospace engineer, space architect\n- Products: V-2 rocket, Saturn V\n\nFacts:\n- Wernher von Braun was born on March 23, 1912, and died on June 16, 1977.\n- Wernher von Braun was a German, later American, aerospace engineer and space architect.\n- Wernher von Braun is credited with inventing the V-2 rocket for Nazi Germany.\n- Wernher von Braun is credited with inventing the Saturn V for the United States.\n- The Applications Technology Satellites were a series of experimental satellites launched by NASA.\n- NASA launched the Applications Technology Satellites under the supervision of, among others, Wernher von Braun.",
